{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":175093,"duration_api_ms":175093,"result":"I'll independently read the two active plans and the S4 freeze, then check hashes, coverage, and design contradictions.The tools plan is in; next I’ll read the game plan in sections and check the frozen hashes.Next I’ll read the remaining WP specs, exceptions, and server/cost sections for DAG and architecture contradictions.**ROLE=independent PLAN_DESIGN critic A**  \n**MODEL=cursor-grok-4.6-xhigh-fast; NO_FALLBACK, NO_COMPOSER, NO_HIDDEN_SUBAGENTS**  \n**REVISION=S4 | PROOF_CLASS=PLAN_DESIGN | PLAN_ONLY**\n\n**Hashes (freeze-s4.json = assigned):**  \nTools SHA256=`f055d2773b01bf6f89cb8a453ebc159af227d7b2158bcc51ad8945d32b39c715`  \nGame SHA256=`48998bde70c53e8e685113f447a3b5b6a6f9bf38a62e1eedb4e218820c5476a4`  \nAggregate=`f9d8a58775db749bd7cfa554f2073d86c099738502a929f42ce5ba50d28bdfae`\n\n**Read coverage:** `zdoc/reviews/20260908-r3/freeze-s4.json`; full tools plan §§0–9, GT-01–10, TQ00–08, TX01–18, `END_OF_TOOLS_PLAN`; full game plan §§0–9, P01–P08, 3.2–3.5, Q00–Q06, H2-P0-01–P9-02, EX01–EX44, `END_OF_GAME_PLAN`. No other plans, critic outputs, or runtime. Both files S4; 10 GT + 32 H2 all `PLANNED`; no `[x]`; `EXECUTION_AUTHORIZATION=PLAN_ONLY`. Cross-file DAG is only GT-10→H2-P0-01.\n\nStock Godot `EditorPlugin`/`EditorUndoRedoManager` plus Blender main-thread `bpy` and an external host journal is a feasible v0.1 automation path. Tools 2.3/2.5 correctly refuse UndoRedo-as-multi-file-atomic and cross-app DB transactions; GT-02 mock lease/journal before GT-03/04 first mutation is the right bootstrap. `studio/**` vs `game/`/`assets-src/` and test-signer ≠ release-signer are coherent. Findings below are closure/DAG defects, not “no software yet.”\n\n---\n\n**P0-1 BLOCKING — Q01-B fixture pulls P2 systems into H2-P1-03**  \n**Where:** game Q01-B L825–827; fixture v1 L840–843; H2-P1-03 L1064–1074.  \n**Scenario:** Keep/kill Godot after P0 bootstrap, before Solo content.  \n**Why insufficient:** One “fixture v1” is shared by B and F and requires walking/emote/outfit avatars, crowded/occluded plaza, **inventory/shop UI**, run/jump, **first activity**, and **enter house**. H2-P1-03 VERIFY is `Q01-B` and forbids primitive-only load. Those behaviors are owned by H2-P2-01…P2-04 (and shop/house UI polish later). Q00 makes the pointed Q-gate the acceptance closure, so P1-03 cannot PASS without P2 deliverables, or else workers must build P2 early under a P1 lease. P0-02 “test IDs per WP” cannot silently shrink Q01 without contradicting §4.  \n**Repair:** Split Q01-B vs Q01-F fixtures. Q01-B = 1 cloned GT-10/look-dev rig × 0/8/32 + plaza walk/turn, no inventory/shop/activity/house. Move those beats to Q01-F / H2-P2-04 / H2-P5-03. Keep “no cubes-only” on the B avatar.\n\n**P0-2 BLOCKING — Q04-L cited whole before block/chat exist**  \n**Where:** game Q04-L L917–922; H2-P1-02 VERIFY L1060–1061; H2-P3-03 VERIFY L1146–1148; owners P4-01 L1162–1169, P4-04 L1191–1198.  \n**Scenario:** 1 dedicated + 2 local clients at the network spike / authority WP.  \n**Why insufficient:** Q04-L is a single paragraph that includes move/emote, ghost cleanup, **and** `logout/block → revoke visibility/chat ≤2s`. P1-02 and P3-03 VERIFY name `Q04-L` with no subset. Chat is off until P4-04; block/AOI is P4-01. Same closure rule as Q00: early WPs inherit a late social contract.  \n**Repair:** Split Q04-L0 (P1-02: move/emote/disconnect ghost/stale session), L1 (P3-03: activity/reward/spoof), L2 (P4-01: block visibility), L3 (P4-04: chat revoke). Point each WP at its slice only.\n\n---\n\n**P1-1 BLOCKING (closure) — EX41 over-assigns 8/32/packed to the 2-client spike**  \n**Where:** game EX41 L1539–1542; H2-P1-02 CONTRACT L1053–1059; Q04-P / H2-P8-02 L945–958, L1310–1318.  \n**Scenario:** Critic applies EX owner lists as Q00 closure.  \n**Why insufficient:** P1-02 is 1 server + 2 clients and empty-process RAM. EX41 also piles `memory 0/8/32` and **packed node** onto P1-02. Packed rooms are explicitly post-v0.1 (L282–283, Q04-P). Two critics can FAIL P1-02 for missing P6/P8 evidence.  \n**Repair:** EX41: P1-02 = empty process/world RAM + dedicated strip + preauth/MTU; 8/32 mem+tick = P6-01; packed node = P8-02.\n\n**P1-2 nonblocking — script/code text mutation has no WP**  \n**Where:** tools 2.3 L192–193; GT-03 L346–352 (nodes/resources only); GT-09 L420–428 (“agent sửa”).  \n**Scenario:** Seeded GDScript fault in conformance, or agent edits `.gd` under the scene writer.  \n**Why insufficient:** Script edits are split from the scene writer, but no GT lists a typed script-edit catalog, parse/import ACK, or `UNSUPPORTED`. GT-09 can be read as requiring script repair.  \n**Repair:** In GT-03/GT-09: scene/resource mutation only; script-text = `UNSUPPORTED` until a named later WP, **or** add that WP with parse/lease/readback before sandbox run.\n\n**P1-3 nonblocking for bootstrap; must fix before P4 — house logout vs 30s hold**  \n**Where:** game P04 L202–207; room hold L344–345; EX44 L1551–1554.  \n**Scenario:** Owner logout while guests/reconnect holds exist.  \n**Why insufficient:** General room rule keeps reconnect reservation 30s inside cap. House v0.1 evicts guests on owner leave and ends the process when holds drain. Occupancy can still count evicted guests as holds, or keep a house process after “closed.”  \n**Repair:** One sentence: owner logout cancels guest holds immediately (only owner reconnect hold optional); cap/process accounting follows that; shop offline remains DB-only.\n\n---\n\n**P2-1 nonblocking — one Android phone blocks all tool handoff**  \n**Where:** tools GT-08 L411–415; TQ08 L496–499; GT-10 depends GT-09→GT-08; game H2-P0-01 L6, L1008–1018.  \n**Why insufficient:** Missing Android is correctly a **target** GAP, but GT-08 cannot ACCEPT and GT-10 cannot ship, so Windows/Linux game bootstrap waits on a phone. P0-02 already allows local game work without every device.  \n**Repair:** GT-10 Windows/Linux package can unlock H2-P0-01…P0-03; Android remains an explicit matrix GAP until GT-08/H2-P1-03.\n\n**P2-2 nonblocking — dual `CURRENT_VALID_WP`**  \n**Where:** tools L17; game L39, L65–66 vs L1729.  \n**Why insufficient:** Both say current = first unticked row. Game current is H2-P0-01 while GT-10 is `PLANNED`. 8.1 A already sequences GT-10 first; the header can still be dispatched as “start game.”  \n**Repair:** Game header: `CURRENT_VALID_WP=H2-P0-01` and `DISPATCHABLE=no until GT-10 ACCEPTED`.\n\n---\n\nNo P0 found on lease/fencing/journal/ACK, path TOCTOU (UNSUPPORTED if no safe-open), package trust (local test key; public sign = P8/P9), asset isolation, or Solo≠Online economy. Proposed 32/room, Q01 ms, and 100M-account gates have owner WPs and pre-consumer locks (P0-02/P3-01/P6/P8). This review does not tick WPs or claim runtime, human, or scale readiness.\n\nVERDICT=REVISE Q01-B and Q04-L are written as single closures that force P2/P4 systems into P1, so the DAG cannot be executed or accepted as specified.","session_id":"fe63550d-47c0-4f9c-a8a5-45704d11c48e","request_id":"09763d89-97d6-4a02-b457-9e42d8e81101","usage":{"inputTokens":90012,"outputTokens":20037,"cacheReadTokens":227840,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
